From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maxim Stepanov <g.maxim.stepanoff@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 12:53:53 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix: clear telemetry-strip clippy residue in dap, editor, and
 zed bin
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

./script/clippy -p database_client (--release --all-targets
--all-features -- --deny warnings) exited 101 because the zedium
telemetry strip left unused variables and dead code in dependency
crates. Underscore-prefix the orphaned locals/params inside stripped
bodies and gate never-called items with allow(dead_code), keeping the
surrounding code intact so upstream merges stay clean.

Sites:
- dap/src/dap.rs: send_telemetry — _location param, _dock,
  _with_build_task, _adapter_name, _kind
- workspace/src/multi_workspace.rs: _side in sidebar context menu,
  open_sidebar, close_sidebar
- workspace/src/pane.rs: emptied `if let Some(_text) =
  telemetry_event_text(..)` bodies (2 sites)
- workspace/src/workspace.rs: emptied `if let Some(_panel) =
  active_panel()` body in toggle_dock
- editor/src/edit_prediction.rs: report_edit_prediction_event — _id
  param, _provider, _extension, _event_type
- editor/src/editor.rs: report_editor_event — _file_extension,
  _vim_mode, _project, _event_type; dropped the no-op
  `if let Saved { auto_saved } {} else {}` and gated the now-unread
  auto_saved field with allow(dead_code)
- zed/src/main.rs: _workspace in handle_open_request (collab strip)
- zed/src/zed/edit_prediction_registry.rs: allow(dead_code) on
  EditPredictionProviderConfig::name

Verified: ./script/clippy -p database_client exits 0;
cargo check -p dap -p editor -p zed clean for these crates;
cargo test -p database_client --lib: 112 passed, 0 failed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MQKuAnEREjToPLedE7KAqP
